    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0552" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1041: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-07T18:00:00+00:00">February 7, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 7—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Department’s telegram No. 29, February 6, 5 p.m. As Boncour<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d476-f1"/> and Massigli<anchor n="7" xml:id="d476-f2"/> are both in
                    Geneva I repeated your telegram to the American Delegation at Geneva and Wilson
                    will take matter up with Boncour this afternoon.</p>
                <p>In addition Marriner<anchor n="8" xml:id="d476-f3"/> called on Leger<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d476-f4"/> who said that there was no question of France’s attitude
                    on the subject and the necessary instruction went forward to Lima yesterday
                    calling Peru’s attention to her obligations under the Briand-Kellogg Pact. They
                    did not specifically support the Brazilian proposal as it was felt that the
                    method of solution was principally a question for the American continents. Word
                    of this action has been sent to Claudel<anchor n="10" xml:id="d476-f5"/>
                    today.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Geneva.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d476-f1" n="6" xml:id="d476-f1-content">
                <p>Joseph Paul-Boncour, French Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d476-f2" n="7" xml:id="d476-f2-content">
                <p>René Massigli, Chief, League of Nations Section, French Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d476-f3" n="8" xml:id="d476-f3-content">
                <p>James Theodore Marriner, Counselor of Embassy in France.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d476-f4" n="9" xml:id="d476-f4-content">
                <p>Alexis Leger, Vice Political Director, French Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d476-f5" n="10" xml:id="d476-f5-content">
                <p>Paul Claudel, French Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
